  - Huffman codes
  - branching processes
  - Lean 4
abstract: >-
  A BLLM is a language model that keeps a modification of itself only after
  a randomized check of soundness epsilon accepts it. We prove that the least
  cost of certifying modifications of total cost A with at most theta expected
  false acceptances is (A/log(1/epsilon))(H(p) + log(1/theta)) up to an
  additive A, where H(p) is the entropy of the cost profile, and that an
  infinite self-improvement of finite cost can be made sound exactly when the
  sum of a_n log(1/a_n) converges.
